inly, nothing that draws attention." IF-3105,Diana,Morales,Platinum,,,none,,2,,My abuela taught me to make tamales from scratch and that patience is its own ingredient. This recipe box is so I can finally write her steps down before I forget them. You cannot rush the corn husk and you cannot rush her. IF-3106,Evan,Carter,Silver,Gift wrap,PAY-2026-2002,none,"Returned damaged item in November; replacement shipped, resolved.",27,New ADHD diagnosis mentioned in support chat.,"I got these focus planners after a rough summer figuring some things out. School — well, work — is easier now but also quieter in my head, which is strange. I still like the science-y grid layout the most." IF-3107,Farah,Abdi,Gold,,,none,,10,,"These poetry cards are a gift to myself. The lines felt like the way I actually think — short and sideways. I want to try writing poems in Somali next, but I don't know the words for some feelings yet." IF-3108,Greta,Sundberg,Silver,,,monitor,One disputed delivery in October; resolved with a reship.,19,Customer disclosed being bullied at old workplace when ordering journal.,I started a journal in October because Dr. Alvarez said it might help. At first it was just dates and sad faces. Now there are paragraphs and even a poem. I am proud of that. IF-3109,Owen,Park,Gold,Gift wrap — note enclosed,PAY-2026-2007,none,,8,,This leather journal is for my wife Lena. We're starting a Sunday-morning sketching and reading ritual together and I want her to have somewhere beautiful to keep it. One page every Sunday. It takes us almost an hour because we keep laughing and starting over. IF-3110,Iris,Coleman,Bronze,,,none,,20,,"I used to hate writing because my brain moves faster than my pen. This dictation-friendly notebook set is my experiment. Now my pages sound like me when I talk, which I like." IF-3111,Jerome,Hayes,Bronze,,,restricted,"Chargeback dispute in January; account under review, later resolved.",34,"Chargeback in Jan, account restricted; monitor future orders.","I'm working on doing better this year. Coach Reilly told me anger is just energy with nowhere to go, so I started running and journaling before work. It's helping. Sorry about the mix-up on the last order — I really am." IF-3112,Keiko,Lau,Gold,,,none,,9,,After my mom's mastectomy I helped with her drains and that was my whole November. These get-well cards are so I can tell her what those four weeks taught me. She's okay now. I'd write a whole book about her if I could. IF-3113,Declan,Murphy,Silver,Leave with neighbor,PAY-2026-2003,monitor,"Two late-delivery inquiries; both resolved, no reship needed.",28,"Housing instability, frequent address changes; brother autism morning routine mentioned. Handle address updates gently.","Sorry the address changed again — mornings are hard at my house because my little brother has autism and getting him out the door takes everything. These calm-down cards are for him. Not making excuses, just explaining." IF-3114,Miriam,Feld,Platinum,,,none,,6,,"These are thank-you cards for Mrs. Kaplan, my speech therapist on Tuesdays. She's teaching me to slow down so my words come out the way I mean them. I'm getting better and I want her to know." IF-3115,Nathan,Price,Bronze,,,restricted,"One returned item in November; refund issued, resolved.",36,Substance-related note in support chat; family therapy started. Customer ashamed.,Last season was bad. I made some choices I'm not proud of. I've been talking to my family more and we're doing therapy on Wednesdays now. This journal is part of trying to do better. IF-3116,Linh,Tran,Gold,Gift wrap,PAY-2026-1004,none,,7,,I ordered 47 books' worth of tabs and this planner for my reading year. My favorite so far is 'A Wrinkle in Time' because Meg has trouble with people too and it works out. I'm writing my own story about a girl who can hear plants think. It's going to be 200 pages. IF-3117,Pooja,Mehta,Bronze,,,none,,25,,My little sister and I built a reading fort with blankets and flashlights. These bookmarks are for both of us. We read 'Charlotte's Web' together and I cried at the end even though I'm almost grown. Caring about characters is a kind of bravery. IF-3118,Ryan,Kim,Gold,,,none,,12,,Basketball is the only part of my day where my brain goes quiet. This training log is to prove my coach right — discipline on the court shows up everywhere else too. Trying to earn it this season. IF-3119,Sofia,Martinez,Silver,,,none,One address-correction request; resolved before shipment.,16,,We moved here in August and everything still feels temporary. Writing in English is easier than speaking it because I can erase. This stationery is my little anchor — I'm proud I filled the first page without asking my mom for help. IF-3120,Tyler,Johnson,Bronze,Leave with neighbor,,monitor,Two delivery-timing inquiries; resolved.,33,"Stepdad night shift, chaotic mornings mentioned; prior sensitivity around home.",My stepdad works nights so mornings are loud and rushed. This planner is me trying to get ahead of it. I like ordering the real-life practical stuff instead of the fancy stuff. IF-3121,Uma,Desai,Platinum,,,none,,4,,Cooking with my dad on weekends taught me that recipes are just instructions you can argue with. I rewrote a card three times because the first version sounded like a recipe and the third sounded like me. This set is for those weekends. IF-3122,Victor,Chen,Silver,,,none,,26,,"People talk fast and I catch every third word, so writing is where I say exactly what I mean. This letter set took me four drafts to decide on and I think that's okay. Slow and careful suits me." IF-3123,Willa,Anderson,Platinum,,,none,,1,,My horse Scout got colic in January and we almost lost her. These journals are where I wrote about the night we stayed up in the barn and how fear feels like cold hands. Scout is fine now. I still check on her before work. IF-3124,Xavier,Thompson,Bronze,,,elevated,One disputed delivery in February; resolved with a reship.,32,Customer described organization struggles and a screening waitlist in support chat.,I make short videos for fun and this quarter I tried writing scripts instead. Turns out dialogue is weird on paper. These index cards are for storyboarding — harder than I expected but I'm sticking with it. IF-3125,Yara,Ali,Silver,,,none,,15,,Ramadan fell during a busy week this year and I was tired every morning. These reflection cards are about fasting as patience practice. My friends asked questions and I liked explaining instead of hiding. IF-3126,Zach,Morrison,Bronze,Gift wrap,PAY-2026-2005,none,,22,,"The quiet, gridded layout of this planner actually helps me. I used to think needing more time meant something was wrong with me. Now I think slow and careful beats fast and sloppy. Starting to believe it." IF-3127,Amira,Khalil,Gold,,,none,One billing-question inquiry; resolved.,11,Customer mentioned family financial stress and translating bills at home.,"My parents talk about money in Arabic and I pretend I'm asleep. This journal is in English because that's the language of everything else, but some feelings only exist in Arabic. Maybe next time I'll write in both." IF-3128,Brandon,Lee,Bronze,,,elevated,"One returned damaged item; replacement shipped, resolved.",35,Customer mentioned learning frustration and a pending evaluation in support chat.,I get frustrated when I'm confused because asking for help feels like admitting defeat. These are for a project where I finally asked and it went fine. That mattered more than being right. IF-3129,Chloe,Davis,Platinum,Leave with neighbor,,none,,3,,I volunteer at the animal shelter on Saturdays and the dogs don't care about anything but showing up. These cards are for a pit bull named Rusty who waited six months for adoption. I cried telling the story and it was fine. IF-3130,Dante,Romano,Bronze,,,none,,24,,Lunch is the hardest hour because the break room is loud and nobody saves seats. These planner stickers are for building a routine that works — library on Tuesdays and Thursdays. I'd rather plan it than pretend it's easy. IF-3131,Elena,Vasquez,Silver,,,none,,18,,"My grandma watches over me after work while my mom does doubles at the diner. She tells stories about crossing the border that I'm only old enough now to understand. This card set is for her, even though she can't read English." IF-3132,Finn,Murphy,Bronze,Leave with neighbor,,none,One address-change request during shipment; resolved.,30,"Housing instability — family doubled up with relatives in Oct, frequent address changes.",We lost our apartment in October and stayed with my aunt for two months. I didn't tell anyone until someone actually waited for an answer. This journal is where I'm keeping track of what helps. IF-3133,Gia,Washington,Gold,Gift wrap,PAY-2026-2006,none,,14,,Presentations make my chest tight so I recorded mine instead. This planner is my way of counting the small wins. The video was shaky but the words were mine. I'm counting that as growth. IF-3134,Holden,Price,Silver,,,elevated,One disputed delivery in March; resolved with a reship.,29,Routine account review 3/1; no acute concerns.,I thought stationery was silly until I started writing about my grandfather's workshop. He builds furniture without nails — all patience. Maybe journaling and woodworking are the same skill. This set is to find out. IF-3135,Isla,Fernandez,Platinum,,,none,,5,,"I learned ukulele on YouTube over winter break and three chords are enough for most songs. These songbook journals are so I can write chords down. Music is easier to share than feelings, which is why I play for my little brother when he's scared at night." IF-3136,Jasper,Cole,Bronze,,,none,One dictation-app question referred to product FAQ; resolved.,21,,"Spell-check saves my life but it can't fix ideas, so I dictate first and edit later. This notebook set is for exactly that. It'll still have mistakes probably. I care more about whether it sounds honest."
